Launceston Half Day Tour

Rates

Per Person - $200.00
Private Charter (4 Guests Max) - $700.00
A light morning or afternoon tea included.

Duration

4 Hours

Itinerary
Pick up from Launceston CBD at 09:00 OR 13:00;
Drop off in Launceston CBD at around13:00 OR 17:00;
Tour Duration approximately 4 hours;
A light morning or afternoon tea included;
Note:- Cellar door tasting fees not included.

Launceston:- Take a tour around Tasmania's second largest city and learn about the early history and view the stunning architecture and open green spaces;
Cataract Gorge:- is a river gorge in Launceston and approximately 1.5 km from the city centre and where the South Esk River flows into the Tamar estuary. It is one of the region's premier tourist attractions and accessible to all ages.
Grindelwald:- Explore the village square and learn about the Dutch man's dream of creating a Swiss-style village;
Brady's Lookout:- Stroll up the small hill for the best view over the Tamar River and across to St Mathias Church at Windemere;
Gin or Wine:- Taste some of these fine liquids en route.
